/**
 * @page topic_platform Platform Services
 * @ingroup module_abstractions
 * @ingroup platform
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section platform_overview Overview
 *
 * ascii-chat consumes platform services from the standalone **libplatform**
 * dependency. The application does not maintain a second in-tree platform
 * layer. Consumers include headers as `<libplatform/foo.h>`.
 *
 * libplatform provides threading and synchronization, sockets, filesystems,
 * terminals and keyboard input, clocks, process helpers, memory, diagnostics,
 * CPU detection, and lifecycle services. ascii-chat owns application policy,
 * media, networking protocols, rendering, and the TUI.
 *
 * @section platform_boundary Ownership and build boundary
 *
 * libplatform owns operating-system implementations and public headers.
 * Application code should use libplatform APIs instead of adding POSIX or Win32
 * calls, compatibility wrappers, or duplicate abstractions.
 *
 * `cmake/dependencies/Libplatform.cmake` configures the dependency from
 * `deps/ascii-chat-deps/libplatform`. Application targets link it through
 * `libplatform::libplatform`. The dependency selects its POSIX, Windows,
 * macOS, Linux, or WASM backend for the active build.
 *
 * @section platform_api API families
 *
 * - `<libplatform/thread.h>`, `<libplatform/mutex.h>`, `<libplatform/rwlock.h>`,
 *   and `<libplatform/cond.h>` provide concurrency primitives.
 * - `<libplatform/socket.h>` provides portable sockets for network transports.
 * - `<libplatform/terminal.h>` and `<libplatform/keyboard.h>` provide terminal
 *   capabilities, raw mode, geometry, and normalized input.
 * - `<libplatform/filesystem.h>`, `<libplatform/system.h>`, and
 *   `<libplatform/process.h>` provide filesystem, process, and system helpers.
 * - `<libplatform/debug/...>` and `<libplatform/symbols.h>` provide diagnostics.
 * - `<libplatform/atomic.h>`, `<libplatform/compiler.h>`, and
 *   `<libplatform/cpu.h>` provide low-level portability support.
 *
 * @section platform_wasm WASM
 *
 * WASM uses libplatform's WASM backend. Browser-specific bindings belong in
 * `src/web` and the shared web packages; they must not reintroduce a parallel
 * browser platform implementation. Browser code uses the same contracts
 * for timing, synchronization, terminal output, and lifecycle behavior.
 *
 * @section platform_testing Testing and changes
 *
 * Change platform behavior in libplatform or its CMake integration, then run
 * the affected ascii-chat contract tests. Do not copy dependency sources into
 * this repository. Source-level smoke tests that compile a backend should
 * reference `deps/ascii-chat-deps/libplatform` explicitly.
 */
